            <ArticleTitle>Traumatic Foreign Body into the Face: Case Report and Literature Review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3487386</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1155/2017/3487386</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper describes a case of mouth opening limitation, secondary to a facial trauma by cutting-piercing instrument, whose fragments had not been diagnosed in the immediate posttrauma care. Description of an unusual surgical maneuver and a literature review are presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
